---
import LegalPageLayout from "@/layouts/LegalPageLayout.astro";
import { useTranslations } from "@/i18n/utils";

const t = useTranslations("en");
const title = t("legal.sale.title");
const description =
  "Terms and conditions of sale and participation for Cloud Native Days France: tickets, refunds, personal data, image rights.";
const lastUpdated = "2026-10-13";
---

<LegalPageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  lang="en"
>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    <em
      >This is a translation of the French <a
        href="/cgv"
        class="text-primary hover:underline"
        >Conditions générales de vente et de participation</a
      >. In case of discrepancy, the French version prevails.</em
    >
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    The Cloud Native Days France conference is organized by the Cloud Native
    France association ("the Organizer"), registered with the Essonne prefecture
    on 17/05/2016, SIRET number 85315583600010.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    All content and events produced by the Cloud Native France association, in
    particular ticket sales and participation in the Cloud Native Days France
    conference, are subject to the General Terms and Conditions.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Purchasing a ticket for the Cloud Native Days France event implies
    acceptance of the Terms and Conditions of Sale.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Participating in Cloud Native Days France, as a speaker or as an attendee,
    even free of charge, implies acceptance of the Terms and Conditions of
    Participation.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">General Terms and Conditions</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    The information published on the websites <a
      href="/en"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">www.cloudnativedays.fr</a
    >, <a
      href="https://billetterie.cloudnativedays.fr/"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">billetterie.cloudnativedays.fr</a
    > and <a
      href="https://cfp.cloudnativedays.fr/2027"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">cfp.cloudnativedays.fr/2027</a
    > is provided subject to the smooth running of the whole event and to the absence
    of last-minute changes. Should the schedule change, the Organizer will do its
    utmost to inform attendees.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Terms and Conditions of Sale</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Prices include VAT. French VAT at 10% applies. Tickets give access to the
    exhibition area, the conference rooms and the catering area.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Each ticket is represented by a personal badge. You may be asked for an ID
    to collect your badge.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Your registration is firm and final. You may however change the name of the
    attendee associated with a ticket by sending a request by email to <a
      href="mailto:billetterie@cloudnativedays.fr"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">billetterie@cloudnativedays.fr</a
    >, until Monday 31 May 2027. After that date, no change of attendee will be
    possible.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    No refund or credit will be issued. A speaker's failure to attend is not
    grounds for a refund or a cancellation.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    The Strategy & Leadership ticket is reserved for people in leadership or
    technical decision-making roles (CEO, CTO, CIO, VP, Head of…). Every
    registration is checked. As an exception to the previous paragraph, the
    Organizer reserves the right to cancel, before the event, any Strategy &
    Leadership ticket whose holder does not match this profile; the amount paid
    is then refunded in full.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    You can pay for your participation by card. We do not accept payment by
    check.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Any order not paid before entering the conference is cancelled. We do not
    accept payment after the conference.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Purchasing a ticket automatically generates an invoice.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Paying for a ticket immediately reserves a seat.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Registering for Cloud Native Days France entails recording your details to
    issue a badge. The data stored are: your first name, last name, email
    address, company, job title, position, employer, seniority, gender, city of
    residence and country of residence. Your phone number may also be stored if
    you consent to it when registering.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    In accordance with data protection law and European regulations, you may
    request access to and/or erasure of your data by email at <a
      href="mailto:billetterie@cloudnativedays.fr"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">billetterie@cloudnativedays.fr</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Your identification badge carries a QR code during the conference. This
    unique code makes it possible, only with your consent, to pass your contact
    details on to our sponsors and exhibitors. Exhibitors at the Cloud Native
    Days France event are allowed to approach you on the day of the conference
    to offer to scan your badge. <strong
      >You remain free to allow or refuse the scan of your badge and the sharing
      of your data with exhibitors</strong
    >. The Organizer cannot be held responsible for the use of your data.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Please report any suspicious solicitation to the Cloud Native Days France
    team, especially outside the exhibition area.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">
    Cancellation or postponement of the event by the Organizer
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    The Organizer, a non-profit association governed by the French law of 1 July
    1901, reserves the right to cancel or postpone the event should
    circumstances compromise its proper organization, its safety or its economic
    viability, in particular in the event of insufficient funding, the default
    of partners or service providers, or force majeure within the meaning of
    Article 1218 of the French Civil Code.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    If the event is postponed, tickets remain valid for the new date offered, at
    no additional cost and with no booking fee. Participants who do not wish to
    take up this postponement may request a refund of their ticket.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    If the event is definitively cancelled, the Organizer may offer Participants
    to keep their ticket for a later edition, subject to their express consent
    and at no additional cost and with no booking fee.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    If this offer is not accepted, or if no new edition is planned, Participants
    may obtain a refund of the sums paid for the unperformed services, in
    accordance with the applicable legal provisions.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Given its non-profit, associative nature, the Organizer will, in the event
    of exceptional financial difficulties, favor seeking amicable solutions with
    Participants, in particular in the form of freely agreed postponements or
    refund schedules, while respecting their statutory rights.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    In the event of cancellation or postponement, the Organizer cannot be held
    liable for indirect costs incurred by Participants, in particular for
    travel, accommodation or meals, where the cancellation or postponement
    results from a case of force majeure or in any other case where its
    liability cannot legally be engaged. Any other claim for compensation will
    be assessed in accordance with applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">
    Terms and Conditions of Participation
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Participation in Cloud Native Days France is possible once your payment has
    been received. Wearing an identification badge is mandatory to access the
    exhibition area and the conference rooms. Anyone without a badge will be
    refused entry. In case of overcrowding, and for safety reasons, the
    Organizer reserves the right to restrict access to conference rooms. The
    house rules of the conference venues apply without reservation to all
    attendees (for example, and without limitation, the ban on smoking in the
    conference areas).
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    Participation in the conference is subject to acceptance of the event's <a
      href="/en/code-of-conduct"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">Code of Conduct</a
    >, available on www.cloudnativedays.fr. The Organizer reserves the right to
    permanently exclude anyone whose behavior or attitude is deemed
    unacceptable, with no entitlement to a refund.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    The Cloud Native Days France event is run in an open spirit that lets
    everyone take part. The Organizer pays close attention to the smooth running
    of the event. Speakers are informed that their talks must not be offensive
    and must respect all attendees. Any breach of decorum, or any incident
    likely to disrupt the conference, must be reported immediately to the
    organizers on site or by email at <a
      href="mailto:billetterie@cloudnativedays.fr"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">billetterie@cloudnativedays.fr</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Image rights</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    When attending Cloud Native Days France as a speaker or attendee, you agree
    to be filmed or photographed. As an attendee, you may appear in group or
    crowd photos; under French law, beyond a certain number of people in a
    photo, your image rights cannot be invoked.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    As a speaker, you agree that your talk will be filmed and recorded. You
    undertake to use only royalty-free content or content for which you have
    acquired the necessary rights (images, music, etc.). You agree that the
    recording of your talk will be published online after the conference.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    All Cloud Native Days France videos are made available under the terms of
    the <a
      href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"
      class="text-primary hover:underline"
      >Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
      License</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Site owner, hosting</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
    The site billetterie.cloudnativedays.fr is hosted by Enix, 40 rue de Cléry,
    75002 Paris. The editorial manager of <a
      href="https://billetterie.cloudnativedays.fr/"
      class="text-primary hover:underline">billetterie.cloudnativedays.fr</a
    > is Jean-Christophe Sirot, vice-president of the Cloud Native France association.
  </p>
</LegalPageLayout>
